# Premium / Luxury Frontend Craftsmanship

Building premium frontend goes beyond functional HTML and CSS — architect immersive digital environments. Apply these standards when the user wants a high-end landing page, interactive portfolio, or component with top-tier visual polish.

## Establish a creative foundation

Don't default to generic, unopinionated code. Commit to one strong visual identity:
- **Editorial Brutalism** — high-contrast monochrome, oversized type, sharp edges, raw grids.
- **Organic Fluidity** — soft gradients, deep rounded corners, glassmorphism, bouncy spring physics.
- **Cyber / Technical** — dark dominance, neon accents, monospaced type, staggered reveals.
- **Cinematic Pacing** — full-viewport imagery, slow cross-fades, deep negative space, scroll storytelling.

## Structural layers for immersion

**Entry sequence.** No blank screen. A lightweight preloader resolves fonts/images/3D, then transitions away fluidly (split-door reveal, scale-up zoom, staggered text sweep).

**Hero architecture.** Full-bleed `100vh`/`100dvh` containers. Break headlines syntactically (wrap by word or character) for cascading entrance animations. Use floating elements or clipping paths for depth behind the copy.

**Fluid navigation.** No static navbars — sticky headers that react to scroll direction (hide on scroll down, reveal on scroll up). Rich hover states (mega-menus with image previews).

## Motion design system

Animation is connective tissue, not afterthought.

**Scroll-driven narratives** (GSAP ScrollTrigger or equivalent): pinned containers that lock while content flows past; vertical-to-horizontal scroll translation for galleries; parallax with varying scroll-speeds across background/midground/foreground.

**High-fidelity micro-interactions:** magnetic buttons (calculate pointer distance, pull toward cursor); custom cursor with lerp interpolation; dimensional hover via `scale`, `rotateX`, `translate3d`.

## Typography & texture

Massive scale contrast — headlines via `clamp()` up to ~`12vw`, body crisp at `16–18px` minimum. Prefer specified variable fonts or premium typefaces over system defaults. Add SVG/CSS noise overlays (`mix-blend-mode: overlay`, opacity `0.02–0.05`) to kill digital sterility. Frosted glass via `backdrop-filter: blur()` plus ultra-thin semi-transparent borders.

## Performance imperative

A beautiful site that stutters is a failure.
- **Composite only** — animate `transform` and `opacity`. Fiercely avoid animating `width`, `height`, `top`, `margin`.
- **`will-change: transform`** intelligently on heavy moving elements; remove post-animation.
- **Responsive degradation** — wrap custom cursor and heavy hover behind `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`.
- **Accessibility** — wrap continuous animation in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`. Never trade accessibility for flair.

## Implementation ecosystem

**React / Next.js:** Framer Motion (layout transitions, spring physics); Lenis (`@studio-freight/lenis`) for smooth scroll; React Three Fiber for WebGL/3D.

**Vanilla / HTML / Astro:** GSAP for timeline sequencing; vanilla Lenis via CDN; SplitType for accessible typography chunking.

## On any "premium / immersive / Awwwards-style" prompt

1. Wrap output in scroll-smoothed architecture.
2. Guarantee performance via composited layers.
3. Integrate staggered component entrances.
4. Elevate typography with fluid scales.
5. Commit to one memorable aesthetic footprint.

